---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Tag from './Tag.astro';
import TechList from './TechList.astro';
import { links } from '../data/site';
import heroMap from '../assets/images/lagos-hero-map.png';
import pipeline from '../assets/images/lagos-pipeline.svg';
import beforeAfter from '../assets/images/lagos-before-after.png';
import candidate from '../assets/images/lagos-candidate-detail.png';

const progress = [
  'Sentinel-1 pair acquired with provenance tracking; preprocessed in ESA SNAP (orbit, calibration, terrain correction)',
  'Backscatter change analysis across 71% of the Lagos study area',
  '400 candidate patches (3.13 km²) with radar and terrain review attributes',
  'Validation against independent evidence (NEMA, GDACS, geolocated imagery) under way',
];

const wide = '(min-width: 1024px) 896px, 100vw';
---

<article id="lagos" class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-10">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
    <Tag>Geospatial pipeline</Tag>
    <Tag tone="progress">In progress</Tag>
  </div>
  <h3 class="mt-4 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">
    Lagos Flood Intelligence — mapping floods from space
  </h3>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-slate-600">
    When heavy rain flooded Lagos on 3–4 July 2024, reports came in from Lekki, Ibeju-Lekki and
    beyond — but no clear map of where the water went. This project builds a reproducible pipeline
    that compares Sentinel-1 radar imagery from before and after an event to find candidate flooded
    areas, with the long-term goal of a reusable runbook for any future flood.
  </p>
  <a href={links.lagosRepo} class="mt-4 inline-block font-medium text-ocean-600 hover:text-ocean-700">
    View on GitHub →
  </a>

  <figure class="mt-8">
    <Image src={heroMap} alt="Map of the Lagos coast with small candidate patches along the coastline and lagoons" widths={[640, 960, 1600]} sizes={wide} class="w-full rounded-lg border border-slate-200" loading="lazy" />
    <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">
      Exploratory Sentinel-1 radar-change candidates (unvalidated), July 2024. Not a confirmed flood extent.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <div>
      <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500">Progress so far</h4>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-slate-700">
        {
          progress.map((item) => (
            <li class="flex gap-2">
              <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-ocean-500" />
              <span>{item}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500">Next</h4>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-slate-700">
        <li>Independent validation and accuracy assessment</li>
        <li>Second event (July 2021)</li>
      </ul>
      <TechList items={['Python', 'GeoPandas', 'ESA SNAP', 'QGIS', 'Sentinel-1/2', 'NASADEM', 'Docker']} />
    </div>
  </div>

  <figure class="mt-10">
    <Image src={pipeline} alt="Workflow: acquire, preprocess, compare, candidates, validate (incomplete)" class="w-full rounded-lg" loading="lazy" />
  </figure>

  <figure class="mt-10">
    <Image src={beforeAfter} alt="Three radar panels of the same area: 21 June 2024, 3 July 2024, and the change between them" widths={[640, 960, 1600]} sizes={wide} class="w-full rounded-lg border border-slate-200" loading="lazy" />
    <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">
      Radar backscatter on 21 June and 3 July 2024, and the change between them.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="mt-10 grid items-start gap-6 lg:grid-cols-5">
    <div class="lg:col-span-2">
      <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold">Why “candidates,” not “floods”</h4>
      <p class="mt-2 text-slate-700">
        A darker radar return doesn’t prove flooding. Each patch is reviewed against terrain,
        historical water, and outside reports before anything is called a flood.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="lg:col-span-3">
      <Image src={candidate} alt="Close-up of candidate C0079 on the eastern margin of Ologe Lagoon with its review attributes" widths={[640, 960, 1200]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 540px, 100vw" class="w-full rounded-lg border border-slate-200" loading="lazy" />
    </figure>
  </div>
</article>
